		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgpfwomus22",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:f64vb5rx6mqokvtn3gbgtnkv/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgp76an222s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3ldgpfwomus22",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T16:05:01.576Z",
			"content": "<p>it’s only been 15+ years of saying the same thing (correctly) 🫠</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:f64vb5rx6mqokvtn3gbgtnkv/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgpvnymi227",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgpfwomus22",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/scottjehl.com/post/3ldgpvnymi227",
			"author": {
				"name": "Scott Jehl",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/scottjehl.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:f64vb5rx6mqokvtn3gbgtnkv/bafkreicwirkhki6y6iujb4eszhob5bfr3plqwlksspvfunewlv7p6djwwi"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T16:13:49.337Z",
			"content": "<p>Well, the recent changes to popularly prioritize server-rendering tells me the work is working! It's just slow because the message runs counter to so many business and developer conveniences, and genuinely a lot of our industry isn't familiar with working any other way now.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgrcht3qc2o",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com/post/3ldgrcht3qc2o",
			"author": {
				"name": "Keith J. Grant",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/bafkreigpjsbjaogf4jwwelrxdt4c5t3jbotfh7eynlqvugf5iwk2sbcbpq"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T16:38:52.813Z",
			"content": "<p>I’d go further and say there’s a contingent that doesn’t really understand the grain of the web at all. I think there’s a chunk of the industry that came in several years ago from more conventional software backgrounds and never really gained that understanding</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:yxpwvgsc62rj6xfo34gd4fo2/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgrs3h6us2y",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/jimmyjazzesq.bsky.social/post/3ldgrs3h6us2y",
			"private": true,
			"date": "2024-12-16T16:47:36.709Z",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgruyy2ec2c",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgrcht3qc2o",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one/post/3ldgruyy2ec2c",
			"author": {
				"name": "Adam Ziolkowski",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/bafkreifeyh3qq5siyq7fq5dbprn5cc3zpouwblh4ticrko3dqkts2526cu"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T16:49:14.782Z",
			"content": "<p>What is the grain of the web in 2024? I ask because I want to know if might need to update my definition which I aquired in early 2000. As for that cohort, I won't deny that there is a large pool of developers that don't have that background and to them React is JS, the web is React...</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgry4oox22c",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgruyy2ec2c",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one/post/3ldgry4oox22c",
			"author": {
				"name": "Adam Ziolkowski",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/bafkreifeyh3qq5siyq7fq5dbprn5cc3zpouwblh4ticrko3dqkts2526cu"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T16:50:59.333Z",
			"content": "<p>but some are seasoned application developers and they find the 'document-based' web lacking in that context... they think in apps, big, fat apps and not just islands of interactivity.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:god7lmgkgqlybavtrf2clc2h/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgv7v3whk2v",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/quirksmode.org/post/3ldgv7v3whk2v",
			"author": {
				"name": "ppk 🇪🇺",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/quirksmode.org",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:god7lmgkgqlybavtrf2clc2h/bafkreibp3m2ycs66haihiby2qli3qajkjabg2ahmz7o2ni5wl5p377q7oa"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T17:49:01.038Z",
			"content": "<p>My question: have these people in power ever before openly acknowledged there is a theory of web development other than their own React/whatever one?</p>\n<p>Is this sort of snipe at normal web dev new? Or are such snipes becoming more common?</p>\n<p>If so ... we're getting somewhere. They're on the defensive.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgwhotg6c2z",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:god7lmgkgqlybavtrf2clc2h/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgv7v3whk2v",
