			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T18:55:40.065Z",
			"content": "<p>if that's who I think it is, it's a great example of a CEO managing to *un*evangelise their service</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:ark7nxcfhgxp4gwdsbzcpnoo/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh2gzqj7c26",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:giyymvrv6yjipdxvlatenrnd/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgnd243qs23",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/autiomaa.org/post/3ldh2gzqj7c26",
			"author": {
				"name": "Daniel Schildt",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/autiomaa.org",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:ark7nxcfhgxp4gwdsbzcpnoo/bafkreidrkmxmq7bqxl6sf2hezydqndwqdtbutmilm7s4mz3a7m2tnlabmi"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T19:22:29.497Z",
			"content": "<p>HTML is so enterprise scalable that it would win awards. 😅</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh2zwtejs2f",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldgruyy2ec2c",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com/post/3ldh2zwtejs2f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Keith J. Grant",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/bafkreigpjsbjaogf4jwwelrxdt4c5t3jbotfh7eynlqvugf5iwk2sbcbpq"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T19:33:03.979Z",
			"content": "<p>I don't really think the grain of the web has changed in any significant ways... it's still progressive enhancement, URL behavior (e.g. using links vs buttons), etc.</p>\n<p>In many ways, it's an understanding that HTML+CSS+JS+SVG is itself a framework and how to work idiomatically within that framework.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh3jfyz3c2c",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh2zwtejs2f",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one/post/3ldh3jfyz3c2c",
			"author": {
				"name": "Adam Ziolkowski",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/bafkreifeyh3qq5siyq7fq5dbprn5cc3zpouwblh4ticrko3dqkts2526cu"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T19:41:43.210Z",
			"content": "<p>In the context of working in larger organizations that create a lot of apps (B2B) there is a LOT of value in using a popular web framework. If an organization doesn't use one, someone will create their own and at that point, more often than not, you'd want to run for the hills.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh4oktzzs2j",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh3jfyz3c2c",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com/post/3ldh4oktzzs2j",
			"author": {
				"name": "Keith J. Grant",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/bafkreigpjsbjaogf4jwwelrxdt4c5t3jbotfh7eynlqvugf5iwk2sbcbpq"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T20:02:29.804Z",
			"content": "<p>Oh I definitely agree.</p>\n<p>There is a lot of value in using a popular web framework, but I think part of that *should* be understanding the underlying web framework it’s built on top of as well.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh4olciwc2j",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh4oktzzs2j",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com/post/3ldh4olciwc2j",
			"author": {
				"name": "Keith J. Grant",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/bafkreigpjsbjaogf4jwwelrxdt4c5t3jbotfh7eynlqvugf5iwk2sbcbpq"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T20:02:29.805Z",
			"content": "<p>Some (though not necessarily all) of the ire aimed at React, for instance, is really a gripe with devs who use React but don’t fully understand the web framework. These are not strictly problems with React at all, but React becomes a lightning rod for those frustrations.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh4qyqwik2c",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh4olciwc2j",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one/post/3ldh4qyqwik2c",
			"author": {
				"name": "Adam Ziolkowski",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/adamz.one",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dlavmrxl5yzs2ads7dsrsovg/bafkreifeyh3qq5siyq7fq5dbprn5cc3zpouwblh4ticrko3dqkts2526cu"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-16T20:03:51.490Z",
			"content": "<p>Yeah, it's the same on the backend side... \"hey, I know Django, I must be a great Python developer\" :)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:vkvvhl5sit6ub7qwixxg2m42/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldhow4f3cc2m",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldh4olciwc2j",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stcbus.bsky.social/post/3ldhow4f3cc2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Steven",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stcbus.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:vkvvhl5sit6ub7qwixxg2m42/bafkreifeqdbyouyor4hn3ttq5gh2oxxfjyfjgrg7homeqbatngxomr3k34"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-17T01:28:50.422Z",
			"content": "<p>Well and all the broken middle clock because the framework is creating links through JavaScript. Oh and it’s slow af.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldhrj6xyr22s",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:vkvvhl5sit6ub7qwixxg2m42/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldhow4f3cc2m",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com/post/3ldhrj6xyr22s",
			"author": {
				"name": "Keith J. Grant",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/keithjgrant.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/bafkreigpjsbjaogf4jwwelrxdt4c5t3jbotfh7eynlqvugf5iwk2sbcbpq"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-17T02:15:18.156Z",
			"content": "<p>The framework doesn’t “make links through JavaScript”. It renders whatever HTML the developer tells it to. If the dev is using event handlers instead of native links, the dev’s own fault</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:vkvvhl5sit6ub7qwixxg2m42/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldhrlhx5ek2j",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:dx7vvynq7d4cwhxd4k4gesck/app.bsky.feed.post/3ldhrj6xyr22s",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stcbus.bsky.social/post/3ldhrlhx5ek2j",
			"author": {
				"name": "Steven",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/stcbus.bsky.social",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:vkvvhl5sit6ub7qwixxg2m42/bafkreifeqdbyouyor4hn3ttq5gh2oxxfjyfjgrg7homeqbatngxomr3k34"
			},
			"date": "2024-12-17T02:16:34.674Z",
			"content": "<p>It’s what the docs (at least previously) showed in tutorials and made the easiest.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
